    ///   `let v = ld32!(c, fr, fm, ADDR, DST, PC, IC, REM);`   `st32!(c, fr, fm, ADDR, VALUE, PC, IC, REM);`   (widths 8 16 32 64 128)
    /// `ADDR`: u32 effective address (lq/sq: the macro rounds it down to 16 like `Fm`). `DST`: the GPR number of the load's destination. `VALUE`: the value to store
    /// (u8..u128). `PC`: the instruction's pc (a plain load/store, NOT in a delay slot). `IC`: instruction count AFTER it (block-start count + index in the block + 1).
